Added :meth:`DeviceData.compare() <peat.data.models.DeviceData.compare>` and :func:`peat.data.compare.compare_device_data`, which return a structured, JSON-serializable diff (added, removed and changed values with readable paths, plus a similarity ratio) between two devices or between a device and exported ``device-data-full.json`` data. Lists of interfaces, services, files, registers and other sub-models are matched by identity keys instead of by position. Values that change on every pull (e.g. ``uptime``, events, the local copies of files) are excluded by default, and comparing makes no network requests. This can be used to detect configuration drift between pulls or to compare a device to a baseline.
